In this patch we corrected some bugs and improved some aspects of the game interface.

Patch notes 1.3

- Fixed the logical bug that did not allow to unlock the Steam trophy "Till death do us part". How to unlock the trophy: [spoiler] The trophy is unlocked playing with Ancoran from the beginning, with a love story with Daragast and coming to besiege Satrapor winning the fight. [/spoiler];

- Correct the writing "Options" in the game;

- Modified the functioning of some Ancoran nodes;

- Modified position and size of the flags used to change language in the initial menu to make them more easily identifiable;

- Corrections of some small bugs.

With this patch we have corrected several bugs and introduced a new management of the audio at double speed.

Patch notes 1.1

- Now the 2X audio is played through a different algorithm that allows the game to distort much less the voice of the narrator;

- Fixed an Ancoran riddle where the answer was wrong;

- Fixed an Ancoran route where you could use the Graystorm even without having unlocked it;

- Fixed the achievement "Puppy" that was only unlocked in one path instead of two;

- Fixed one of Leon's final enigmas in the path of the elements;

- Fixed many other small bugs.

Thank you so much for the reports you sent us!

The moment has finally come, version 1.0 is online for Windows and Mac OS! 
Also, you can find a demo to try the game! 

Here's what we introduced:
- Implemented the Trophy and Missions system. By completing a mission you receive an artwork of the work in progress of the game as a reward;
- Introduction of various animations within game backgrounds;
- Insertion of new nodes and a lot of new resources within the game;
- Insertion of animations in the game menu;
- Animation optimization for all supported resolutions;
- Revised the internal management of the game interface to make it compatible with new animations;
- Now animations pause when you enter the game options;
- Change to the algorithm for managing page movement;
- Improved button operation in options;
- Correction in the translations of the buttons;
- Fixed a bug in the difficulty "Hesperia Legend" which involved the exclusion of the save slot;
- Elimination of some debugging code no longer needed to improve performance;
- Small spoiler [spoiler]Corrected the path of Ancoran where the dragon was still present, although it had not been captured by Leon during the Prologue;[/spoiler]
- Changed the default quality of Unity from Very Low to Ultra, it can still be modified before entering the game. We advise you to always try to play in Ultra, the game is very light;
- Fixed a lot of paths and minor bugs.

We have tested the game a lot but something could have escaped us, if you find any bugs, please let us know in the Steam discussion! :)

We are happy to announce that we are completing the latest works before the release from the Early Access.
We will release the final version of the game on Friday, February 15th at 6 pm UTC+1.

On the current public build, the structure that manages the interaction of the nodes is final, if you find bugs as missing choices that do not allow you to continue, please report it to us!


What are we working on?

- Addition of missions and trophies. Each trophy will unlock an unprecedented image of the work on the game as a reward. The panel opens on the last character used;

- Work on animations. We have added animations in the menu and in the pre-selection of the character. We are currently working on animations of game backgrounds;

- Added the ability to insert and remove animations in real time from the menu;

- Update of the save button, will show how many nodes are missing to save depending on the difficulty;

- Correction of the operation of some buttons;

- Correction of the translation of some panels;

- Lastly, we will proceed with all the necessary tests before release.

All this and many other improvements will be introduced in the February 15th patch.

Very little is missing!

https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/33493375/b4efa559e9b1fb115229f16aad8af592c010e5e6.jpg

With this patch we introduced the second game mode (Explorer), audio management buttons outside the book and many other things.

Patch notes  0.7.0

- Introduced the Explorer game mode, unlockable ending a campaign in standard mode. By selecting this mode, you will have an infinite amount of Fate.
By selecting Standard or Explorer mode and combining it with the difficulties, you will be able to get the experience that best suits your needs;

- Added audio management buttons even when the book is closed. This way you can play without using the book;

- Updated the operating logic for the management of audio buttons in the book and outside the book;

- Added the ability to turn the pages of the book using the keyboard;

- Fixed and added some environmental sound effects;

- Fixed an Ancoran path that showed no choices after the clash with Leon;

- Added a panel showing the character used previously when selecting a new character during the same campaign;

- Added text to better explain certain passages after death or reaching a final;

- Fixed some bugs in the tutorial;

- Fixed some minor bugs.

With this patch we went to correct decision-making paths, unlocking a new one.

Patch notes 0.6.0

- Added an Ancalimo path accessible only in case of revenge and on condition that it was also played Daragast;

- Fixed bugs that led to a blank screen after the click of some choices;

- The thank you screen was introduced in place of any white screens that may still be present. No white screens emerge from our tests;

- Fixed a bug introduced with the latest patches where the text of some choices was no longer present.

- Introduced environmental sounds, currently under test. In particular, we are evaluating the default volume according to the music track. The game deals with environmental sounds separately from music and voice. You can increase or decrease the sound effect bar through the options to better adjust the atmosphere.

- Fixed some minor bugs.

Patch notes 0.5.2

- reactivated the special musical track present in the Credits;
- correct the audio of two choices at the beginning of the Daragast story;
- fixed an end of Leon where the story was not heard in Italian;
- some minor fixes to texts in English, especially in the new contents of the patch 0.5.0;
- first tests on the tutorial (currently deactivated).

Here we are with the biggest update since the beginning of the Early Access!

From now on the game will be playable from start to finish with all 4 characters and through all decision-making paths.

Patch Notes:

- Unlocked all decision-making paths and their respective endings;
- The 40 achievements are now available;
- 3D Tune-In inserted and optimized;
- Insert new music tracks, images, audio tracks, icons and much more!
- Improved keyboard and controller game management;
- New internal file management method;
- Fixed several minor bugs and missing files.

What will we work on in the next few weeks?

- Fix any bugs;
- Interactive tutorial;
- Demo;
- Adding more animations for game backgrounds;
- Second game mode;
- Trophies and missions.

For now it's all, if you find any bugs, do not hesitate to write in the forum! :)

The 32-bit Windows version will be available tomorrow, while the Mac OS will be available in the coming days.

Here is a brief update on the progress of the works.

At the moment in the internal testing version we loaded more than 10,600 audio files and more than 800 illustrations.

Unity does not seem to like so much data, so we asked Ancalimo to do a "friendly visit" to help him think better.

According to our tests within the game are missing about 0.006% of the data, a low number but that we will continue to decrease with the next patches.

Given the amount of data, we are working on an update system that is as light as possible and that allows you to download the least amount of data to each corrective patch.

We expect to release the patch on Tuesday, December 18th. Much will depend on the tests of these days.

What you will find in the next patch:
- The adventure will be playable from start to finish;
- We have included all the music tracks, all the images, the narrations and the texts;
- 3D Tune-In: applied to music, text and choices. It allows to improve the experience of those with hearing problems;
- Complete navigation from controller and keyboard;
- Introduced the search panel in the book, reachable by clicking the magnifying glass. Allows you to find the point where the narrator is, typing one of the last words heard.

With this patch we focused in particular on the game options and the preparation of the patch that will bring 100% content.

Patch notes:

- Anti-spoiler system of choices, you can decide whether to show the choices: right away (as now), immediately after the end of the narrative or at your click. At the beginning of the campaign it is possible to select one of these options, as well as during one of the saves already created;

- Editable game controls for keyboard and controller (in the menu and option selection screens are currently being tested and are disabled);

- Added customization options within the game session;

- Change of most of the game panels; 

- Added brightness and gamma options; 

- Ability to select the size of the text of the book and the choices; 

- Option to decide whether to memorize the last position of the book; 

- Introduced the video of "Tary Meldon and Era" once met;

- Game credits with an exclusive musical track!

- 3D Tune-in implemented and currently undergoing internal testing;

- Text search tool in the book being tested internally.

In this brief update I will explain how we have divided the contents of the next two big patches and the timing.  

Patch 1 - Controls and options  

In the first patch that will probably be released on Friday, November 30th, we will show you:  

- Editable game controls for keyboard and mouse;  

- Anti-spoiler system of choices, you can decide whether to show the choices right away (as now), immediately after the end of the narrative or at your click;  

- Change of most of the game panels;  

- Brightness and range adjustment;  

- Ability to select the size of the text of the book and the choices;  

- Option to decide whether to memorize the last position of the book;  

- Game credits with an exclusive musical track!

Patch 2 - Game content and options  

We still need 15 days for this patch. Recording studios are analyzing all the audio files for errors. The amount of work is really great considering that 40 hours are spoken by la, therefore, indicated to take a few extra days to make sure that the work is done at its best. It would not make sense to release the patch earlier but with errors. I hope you will agree with me!  

Here's what we will include in this patch:  

- Update of all audio tracks and addition of new audio tracks;  

- Unlock of the whole adventure, you will be able to play all the 2000 decision nodes;  

- Images, videos, texts, music and icons necessary for new decision-making nodes;  

- 40 achievements covering the 4 characters and "generic" situations such as the number of scenes visited and the deaths of the characters.

After these patches we will:

- Continue the tests on the game in order to find any bugs;  

- Introduce the interactive tutorial;  

- Work on the second game mode;  

- Add a demo with Leon's prologue;

- Complete the "Trophies and missions" section.  

For now it's all, we will publish detailed patch updates as they become available!

In these 9 days we have been working on several implementations in parallel, some are present in this update but others require further testing and will be included in future updates!


What we are working on


- Demo;

- Achievements;

- Keyboard and controller commands with default and reconfigurable settings (controller confirmed: our tests for default commands are on XBox One and PS4 controllers);

- Insertion of some of the material in preparation of the November patch where we will bring the material to 100%, at the moment the new data is locked;

- Testing all the stories and plots in view of the November patch;

- 3D Tune-In, we are inserting and testing this feature that allows those who use hearing aids or have auditory/visual problems to reap benefits while playing;

- Tutorial: narrated and interactive, through the tutorial we will explain several "obscure" TBS mechanics and explain how to use the game interface;

- New environmental sound effects;

- Different features such as: no spoiler of the choices until the end of the narration, open/closed book by default and many others.


Updates of version 2.1.0

- Download of new data in preparation for the November patch;

- Update playable nodes with the correction of some links to other nodes;

- Fixed a bug that led to a wrong position of the loading panel causing a freezing of the game in some cases of death, final or selection of a new character;

- Replaced text in Character Selection for frequency saving of hell (0) with "-";

- Centred description text difficulty of the panel that appears on over the difficulty in the  pg selection;

- Correction of some minor bugs.
